{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSToolBarTop","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSToolBarTop\/init(title:hasLargeTitle:subtitle:leadingItems:principalItem:trailingItems:)"],"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers","generated":true},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSToolBarTop\/body(content:)"],"anchor":"Instance-Methods","title":"Instance Methods","generated":true},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSToolBarTop\/ViewModifier-Implementations"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Default-Implementations","title":"Default Implementations"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/7SwiftUI12ViewModifierP"],"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To"}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"struct","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"OUDSToolBarTop","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","platforms":[{"deprecated":false,"name":"iOS","introducedAt":"15.0","unavailable":false,"beta":false},{"deprecated":false,"name":"iPadOS","introducedAt":"15.0","unavailable":false,"beta":false},{"deprecated":false,"name":"Mac Catalyst","introducedAt":"15.0","unavailable":false,"beta":false},{"deprecated":false,"name":"visionOS","introducedAt":"1.0","unavailable":false,"beta":false}],"externalID":"s:14OUDSComponents14OUDSToolBarTopV","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"OUDSToolBarTop"}],"title":"OUDSToolBarTop","modules":[{"name":"Components"}]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/oudscomponents\/oudstoolbartop"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The top toolbar (aka ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"navigation bar"}]},{"type":"text","text":" on iOS and iPadOS 18 and lower) sits at the top of the screen and provides contextual information"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and controls related to the current view."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"It typically displays the page title, and may include navigation actions such as “Back” or “Close” as well as supplementary actions."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"It can contain leading, principal (center, single item only), and trailing actions.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@"},{"text":"MainActor","kind":"attribute","preciseIdentifier":"s:ScM"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"OUDSToolBarTop","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Warning"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": If an item is placed in principal position, the subtitle is never displayed (whatever "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hasLargeTitle"},{"text":" is), because","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".principal"},{"type":"text","text":" placement only replaces the inline compact bar title, not "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".navigationSubtitle()"},{"text":" (iOS 26+), which would","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"otherwise keep rendering next to the item with no visible title next to it. The title itself is displayed only if ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hasLargeTitle"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":" (in that case it appears below the bar, in large title mode, not inside it)."}]},{"anchor":"Appearances","level":2,"text":"Appearances","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"With Liquid Glass \/ iOS 26+ the OS will change the rendering of the toolbar items depending to the context:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The OS can group the items of same types in one group with kind of rectangle (e.g. views with menus)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"But for buttons items they will remain isolated"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The placement of the title can be leading or centered depending to the length of the text","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The text can be truncated if there is not enough remaining space"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The OS can apply another style for the back button","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Without Liquid Glass \/ iOS 18 and lower, the OS won’t change that much the style of the toolbar items, Items won’t be visually grouped.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The appearance of navigation bar elements is changed by the ","type":"text"},{"code":"oudsNavigationBarAppearance","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"View"},{"type":"text","text":" helper, which must be applied to the root view of the "},{"code":"NavigationStack","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"text":"Technical constraints","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Technical-constraints"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To ensure the back button and text use the correct color on iOS 18 and earlier, apply the following accent color in your main view:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["    struct AppMainView: View {","        var body: some View {","            ContentView()","                .accentColor(theme.colors.contentDefault)","        }","    }"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Platform considerations","anchor":"Platform-considerations"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The component is available on iOS, iPadOS, and visionOS"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The component is not available for watchOS, tvOS and macOS","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Badges uses","level":2,"anchor":"Badges-uses"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For iOS 26 with Liquid Glass, the system badge is used because the OUDS badge component does not provide a suitable","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rendering with the glassified effect applied on the top toolbar.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"For iOS until 18 and without Liquid Glass  OUDS badge component is always used."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Code-sample","type":"heading","text":"Code sample"},{"code":["    ContentView()","        .toolBarTop(\"Title\",","            leadingItems: {","                OUDSToolBarItem(navigation: .back())","            },","            principalItem: OUDSToolBarItem(icon: Image(decorative: \"search\"), accessibilityLabel: \"Search\") { \/* Action to process *\/ },","            trailingItems: {","                OUDSToolBarItem(label: \"Label\") { \/* Action to process *\/ }","                OUDSToolBarItem(icon: Image(decorative: \"some_image\"), accessibilityLabel: \"Label\") { \/* Action to process *\/ }","            }","        )"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"code":"View","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" helper can also be used to apply a SwiftUI toolbar configuration."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["    toolBarTop(_:hasLargeTitle:subtitle:leadingItems:principalIt